04:45:07,420 --> 04:45:09,320
Rep. Julienne "Jam" L. Baronda: Maraming salamat, Mr. Speaker.

3786
04:45:09,980 --> 04:45:21,440
Rep. Julienne "Jam" L. Baronda: This representation, Mr. Speaker, once again requests this august body to consider the proposed budget of the Department of Human Settlements and Urban Development,

3787
04:45:21,440 --> 04:45:34,840
Rep. Julienne "Jam" L. Baronda: National Housing Authority, Social Housing Finance Corporation, and National Home Mortgage Financing Corporation for the consideration of this honorable body.

3788
04:45:35,440 --> 04:45:37,440
Deputy Speaker Vincent Franco "Duke" D. Frasco: Thank you very much. Majority Leader?

3789
04:45:38,000 --> 04:45:51,240
Rep. Alyssa Michaela "Mica" M. Gonzales: Mr. Speaker, I move to recognize Representative Iris Marie Demesa Montes of 4K Party-list to interpellate the sponsor on the proposed budget of the Department of Human Settlements and Urban Development.

3790
04:45:51,420 --> 04:45:57,000
Deputy Speaker Vincent Franco "Duke" D. Frasco: Representative Montes is recognized to interpellate the sponsor. You have 30 minutes.

3791
04:45:57,000 --> 04:46:03,340
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Thank you, Mr. Speaker. Magandang hapon po, distinguished colleagues at mga kasama sa DHSUD.

3792
04:46:04,920 --> 04:46:12,480
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Salamat po sa ating sponsor sa kanyang sponsorship speech sa budget po ng D-SUDE.

3793
04:46:12,980 --> 04:46:16,240
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Napakarami pong impormasyon, napakaraming numero.

3794
04:46:16,240 --> 04:46:24,280
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: So, gusto ko po sanang maunawaan, isimplify, maintindihan po yung mga sinabi ninyo.

3795
04:46:24,640 --> 04:46:30,240
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: So, please allow me, kung maaari po, umpisahan natin ang aking mga katanungan.

3796
04:46:32,960 --> 04:46:37,320
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Una po, ano po ang actual housing need po natin?

3797
04:46:37,900 --> 04:46:45,440
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Let's start po. Ano po ang kailangan, numero ng pabahay na kailangan natin sa ngayon?

3798
04:46:46,240 --> 04:46:56,280
Rep. Julienne "Jam" L. Baronda: Based on 24, on this date is 3.77 million po, Mr. Speaker.

3799
04:46:57,320 --> 04:47:03,240
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: So, yan po ang pangangailangan. Ano naman po ang backlog natin sa ngayon?

3800
04:47:06,000 --> 04:47:11,000
Rep. Julienne "Jam" L. Baronda: Ang backlog po natin ngayon, as of this date, is 2.2 million.

3801
04:47:11,640 --> 04:47:13,500
Rep. Julienne "Jam" L. Baronda: 2.2 million.

3802
04:47:13,500 --> 04:47:21,780
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Ano naman po ang actual na na-construct na natin sa ngayon, as we speak?

3803
04:47:21,800 --> 04:47:29,820
Rep. Julienne "Jam" L. Baronda: Ang sinabi ko po lahat, based on the recent, 136,000.

3804
04:47:32,640 --> 04:47:33,240
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: 136,000.

3805
04:47:33,240 --> 04:47:34,780
Rep. Julienne "Jam" L. Baronda: Sa iba't-ibang...

3806
04:47:34,780 --> 04:47:36,040
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Yes po, housing units.

3807
04:47:36,060 --> 04:47:36,900
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Housing units.

3808
04:47:36,900 --> 04:47:43,380
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Out of the 136,000 na na-construct po, I suppose these are ready for occupancy.

3809
04:47:43,500 --> 04:47:44,020
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Tama po?

3810
04:47:44,320 --> 04:47:45,180
Rep. Julienne "Jam" L. Baronda: Yes po.

3811
04:47:45,460 --> 04:47:51,980
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Out of this po, ilan naman po dito ang actual na po na-ocupa?

3812
04:47:52,720 --> 04:47:56,640
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: I mean, na-turnover na po natin out of the 136,000?

3813
04:47:59,920 --> 04:48:02,640
Rep. Julienne "Jam" L. Baronda: Based po sa...

3814
04:48:07,440 --> 04:48:12,640
Rep. Julienne "Jam" L. Baronda: 11,000...

3815
04:48:13,500 --> 04:48:20,460
Rep. Julienne "Jam" L. Baronda: 700 beneficiary families has successfully availed dowsing units under this program.

3816
04:48:21,560 --> 04:48:21,940
Rep. Julienne "Jam" L. Baronda: So...

3817
04:48:21,940 --> 04:48:25,980
Rep. Julienne "Jam" L. Baronda: So, kasi, Madam, Mr. Speaker, yung iba kasi CMP.

3818
04:48:26,640 --> 04:48:32,200
Rep. Julienne "Jam" L. Baronda: So, ito yung occupants, yung bahay na sinasabi, or units, ito po yun.

3819
04:48:32,640 --> 04:48:32,940
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Okay.

3820
04:48:32,940 --> 04:48:43,320
Rep. Julienne "Jam" L. Baronda: Pero with CMP, with the mortgage out of the program, 136,000 po lahat, beneficiaries, Mr. Speaker.

3821
04:48:43,500 --> 04:48:57,680
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: So, kung ipuporsyento po natin, ano, out of the current 2.2 backlog, we have actually constructed about 136,000 housing units.

3822
04:48:57,840 --> 04:49:01,680
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: So, that's just about ilang porsyento po ito.

3823
04:49:02,340 --> 04:49:06,760
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Wala pa po ito sa 10%, roughly 6%, am I correct?

3824
04:49:08,580 --> 04:49:10,640
Rep. Julienne "Jam" L. Baronda: Actually, Mr. Speaker, okay.

3825
04:49:11,440 --> 04:49:13,160
Rep. Julienne "Jam" L. Baronda: Kasi this is under the new modality.

3826
04:49:13,500 --> 04:49:17,520
Rep. Julienne "Jam" L. Baronda: Dati na 4-page program, iba yun.

3827
04:49:17,780 --> 04:49:19,260
Rep. Julienne "Jam" L. Baronda: It's impossible to do.

3828
04:49:19,860 --> 04:49:26,040
Rep. Julienne "Jam" L. Baronda: Kaya po ginagawa natin because we have to also consider yung naka-pipeline pa.

3829
04:49:26,520 --> 04:49:33,580
Rep. Julienne "Jam" L. Baronda: In short po, with these new modalities, from 7, naging dalawa na lang.

3830
04:49:33,600 --> 04:49:37,080
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Yes, I understand po, Madam Sponsor. Pasensya na po.

3831
04:49:37,180 --> 04:49:43,260
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Gusto ko lang muna pong ilatag yung ating mga numero so that later on when we discuss this,

3832
04:49:43,500 --> 04:49:47,360
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: we are on the same page whether we change our modalities or not.

3833
04:49:47,800 --> 04:49:55,040
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: We agree that ito po yung kakulangan, ito ang ginagawa, para lang po madali yung discussion.

3834
04:49:55,700 --> 04:50:02,460
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: So, we have about, out of the 2.2 million backlog, we have constructed about 136,000,

3835
04:50:02,460 --> 04:50:06,020
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: which is roughly 6% of the actual backlog, am I correct? Tama po ba?

3836
04:50:07,120 --> 04:50:12,460
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: And out of the actual construction, we have delivered roughly 11%.

3837
04:50:12,460 --> 04:50:13,860
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Tama po?

3838
04:50:13,860 --> 04:50:17,960
Rep. Julienne "Jam" L. Baronda: Yes, but Mr. Speaker, I would just like to inform Congresswoman for,

3839
04:50:18,420 --> 04:50:26,280
Rep. Julienne "Jam" L. Baronda: that the proposed deliverables by 2028 are 1.1 million units

3840
04:50:26,280 --> 04:50:32,440
Rep. Julienne "Jam" L. Baronda: from direct and indirect housing provision. Units po, I'm sorry, units po, from direct and indirect.

3841
04:50:33,700 --> 04:50:37,620
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: That's a little bit perspective, Madam Sponsor, Mr. Speaker.

3842
04:50:37,620 --> 04:50:41,620
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: I don't like to look at 2028.

3843
04:50:42,460 --> 04:50:48,460
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Because I have not established what is 2026, and I have not yet foreseen 2027.

3844
04:50:49,300 --> 04:51:02,280
Rep. Julienne "Jam" L. Baronda: Mr. Speaker, we do have the numbers of 588,700 indirect po and direct housing provisions to this date.

3845
04:51:03,540 --> 04:51:06,900
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Okay po, sige po. I'll leave the figures of that first.

3846
04:51:08,600 --> 04:51:12,000
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: I'll just shift, move on to another topic muna po.

3847
04:51:12,460 --> 04:51:13,560
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Ito po, ito mamaya.

3848
04:51:14,100 --> 04:51:17,440
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Tama po ba, ito may mga, itong mga nakalipas na taon,

3849
04:51:17,580 --> 04:51:21,660
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: ang disud ay nabatikos dahil sa mababang utilization rate?

3850
04:51:21,860 --> 04:51:25,040
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Tama po ba ang pagkakaalam ko?

3851
04:51:25,620 --> 04:51:29,620
Rep. Julienne "Jam" L. Baronda: Yes, tama po yun. Dahil po, mababang ang 4PH at saka yung interest subsidy.

3852
04:51:30,140 --> 04:51:37,900
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Opo, kasi from 700 million na dati sa 4PH, naging 35 million na lang po ba?

3853
04:51:37,900 --> 04:51:42,180
Rep. Julienne "Jam" L. Baronda: Madam, Mr. Speaker, kaya po,

3854
04:51:42,460 --> 04:51:49,780
Rep. Julienne "Jam" L. Baronda: yung 1,100 units lang, if I'm not mistaken, dahil po, sa isang modality lang.

3855
04:51:49,900 --> 04:51:56,700
Rep. Julienne "Jam" L. Baronda: Ngayon, we expanded it to many modality. Kaya po, nagka-problema talaga tayo previous years.

3856
04:51:57,060 --> 04:52:04,900
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: The reason being cited by the SUDOS, the reason that there was underutilization of us,

3857
04:52:04,900 --> 04:52:10,260
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: because there was only one modality that was being implemented. Correct po, yan po ang daylan.

3858
04:52:10,340 --> 04:52:12,300
Rep. Julienne "Jam" L. Baronda: Yes, in short, Mr. Speaker, hindi nagamit.

3859
04:52:12,460 --> 04:52:23,580
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: So, partly because of that, you have actually learned your lesson from there and you wanted to expand to more modalities. Am I correct po?

3860
04:52:24,320 --> 04:52:26,960
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Okay po. Sige po. Maraming salamat po.

3861
04:52:27,300 --> 04:52:41,520
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: And that, in the coming years, we shall await your commitment na ma-deliver po yung mga commitments ninyo under the 4PH program. Is that correct also?

3862
04:52:41,520 --> 04:52:42,860
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Madam Sponsor,

3863
04:52:42,860 --> 04:52:43,500
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Mr. Speaker?

3864
04:52:49,060 --> 04:52:58,360
Rep. Julienne "Jam" L. Baronda: Mr. Speaker, yung target po natin is 1,130,676, to be exact, direct and indirect po.

3865
04:52:58,480 --> 04:53:06,220
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: For 2020, eh tama po. So, that would still be a backlog, half of our current backlog, tama po?

3866
04:53:06,640 --> 04:53:08,000
Rep. Julienne "Jam" L. Baronda: Yes, Mr. Speaker.

3867
04:53:08,000 --> 04:53:12,400
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: And since dumadami po tayo.

3868
04:53:12,460 --> 04:53:17,660
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: So, I'm certain that in 2028, yung backlog na yan madadagdagan na naman.

3869
04:53:17,960 --> 04:53:18,440
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Tama po?

3870
04:53:18,500 --> 04:53:22,320
Rep. Julienne "Jam" L. Baronda: 3.7 po by 2028 yung sinabi ko po kanina, Madam Speaker.

3871
04:53:22,400 --> 04:53:24,280
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Ah, so itong figure niyo po by 2028 na figure po ito?

3872
04:53:24,280 --> 04:53:24,740
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Yes po.

3873
04:53:24,880 --> 04:53:25,120
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Okay.

3874
04:53:25,660 --> 04:53:33,900
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: So, ang commitment po ng DSUD by 2028, you would have delivered 1.1 million in housing units actually.

3875
04:53:34,080 --> 04:53:35,000
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Yes po, Mr. Speaker.

3876
04:53:35,480 --> 04:53:36,300
Rep. Julienne "Jam" L. Baronda: Direct and indirect.

3877
04:53:36,660 --> 04:53:37,120
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Sige po.

3878
04:53:37,120 --> 04:53:48,880
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: So, I'll trust that prospective po itong pag-realize natin ng ating commitments for our housing.

3879
04:53:49,140 --> 04:54:00,480
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: So, I will wait until next year siguro po to check on our progress with regard to addressing our housing backlog.

3880
04:54:00,680 --> 04:54:01,500
Rep. Julienne "Jam" L. Baronda: Yes, Mr. Speaker.

3881
04:54:01,640 --> 04:54:04,100
Rep. Julienne "Jam" L. Baronda: Remember po, last time, 1,100 lang.

3882
04:54:04,540 --> 04:54:05,800
Rep. Julienne "Jam" L. Baronda: Ngayon, it's just less than a year.

3883
04:54:05,800 --> 04:54:06,920
Rep. Julienne "Jam" L. Baronda: A year, it's almost.

3884
04:54:07,120 --> 04:54:08,560
Rep. Julienne "Jam" L. Baronda: 136,000 po.

3885
04:54:09,340 --> 04:54:12,440
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Maraming salamat po, Madam Sponsor, Mr. Speaker.

3886
04:54:12,960 --> 04:54:17,180
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Moving on to another topic, ito po ang mga housing units natin.

3887
04:54:18,680 --> 04:54:25,480
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: I remember po, si President Marcos made a pronouncement, in fact, a directive.

3888
04:54:26,140 --> 04:54:34,580
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: He directed agencies to pursue sariling kuryente, I think during his SONA, para sa households, for our households.

3889
04:54:34,580 --> 04:54:36,580
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: How does your 2027 budget?

3890
04:54:37,120 --> 04:54:39,340
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: How does your 2027 budget now operationalize this directive?

3891
04:54:39,340 --> 04:54:46,500
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Nakasama po ba yan dyan sa mga plano ninyo pong mga modalities, whatever modalities you have right now?

3892
04:54:47,380 --> 04:54:52,100
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Is it, ano po, integrated na ang directive ng sariling kuryente?

3893
04:54:52,660 --> 04:54:55,620
Rep. Julienne "Jam" L. Baronda: To be honest po, Mr. Speaker, wala po tayo.

3894
04:54:55,700 --> 04:55:05,160
Rep. Julienne "Jam" L. Baronda: But we, nag-usap, nagpag-usap tayo with the CMP and National Executive, NIA po, natulungan tayo.

3895
04:55:05,160 --> 04:55:05,540
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Yes.

3896
04:55:07,120 --> 04:55:17,080
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Alam din naman natin ang kahalagahan nitong direktiba ng Pangulo, lalo na sa panahong napakataas ng presyo ng kuryente,

3897
04:55:17,860 --> 04:55:22,260
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: ang mga housing units po yan ay uutangin ng mga ordinaryong mamamayan.

3898
04:55:23,000 --> 04:55:28,520
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Kung meron po, naka-integrate po sa plano ng DSUD, ang mga solar-ready homes,

3899
04:55:28,520 --> 04:55:36,260
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: malaking kapakinabangan po yan sa mga ordinaryong pamilya na makabawa sa kanilang pang-araw-araw na gastusin.

3900
04:55:37,120 --> 04:55:41,720
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Ngayon, ma-idagdag yan sa mga amortisasyon ng pabahay na kanilang kinipunta.

3901
04:55:41,720 --> 04:55:47,420
Rep. Julienne "Jam" L. Baronda: Mr. Speaker, in as much as the Department 1 na isama yan, pero ngayon may good news tayo.

3902
04:55:47,920 --> 04:55:51,880
Rep. Julienne "Jam" L. Baronda: Kasi yung mga solar panels construction, inalaw na po ng pag-ibig.

3903
04:55:52,720 --> 04:55:57,660
Rep. Julienne "Jam" L. Baronda: So, ito very, parang lowest rate kasama na po sa loan nila, Mr. Speaker.

3904
04:55:57,660 --> 04:56:02,760
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Yes po, but that is still, that's another matter, Mr. Speaker, medyo prohibitive pa rin ang cost.

3905
04:56:02,860 --> 04:56:06,460
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Ang sinasabi ko lang po dito, kung mga socialized housing po,

3906
04:56:07,120 --> 04:56:10,960
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: ganda nga solar-ready yung mga socialized housing natin,

3907
04:56:11,260 --> 04:56:17,600
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: para hindi na po i-be-bear nung mga mahihirap yung gastusin para doon.

3908
04:56:17,980 --> 04:56:23,160
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: So, ang akin lang pong concern is, kung wala pa man po sa plano ngayon ng DSUD yan,

3909
04:56:23,160 --> 04:56:28,400
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: baka sakali po sa mga susunod na taon, yan naman po ang ating aasikasuhin

3910
04:56:28,400 --> 04:56:33,880
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: because I know for a fact that there's already a private company, housing company,

3911
04:56:34,260 --> 04:56:36,280
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: that's in fact successfully built.

3912
04:56:37,120 --> 04:56:45,900
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Some is a housing project somewhere in Cavite and another one in Pampanga yata na fully solar panel na po.

3913
04:56:46,000 --> 04:56:50,160
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: If they can do it, baka it's a step towards a good direction,

3914
04:56:50,620 --> 04:56:56,780
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: maisama na rin po ng DSUD sa mga future modalities na inyo pong ginagawa.

3915
04:56:56,780 --> 04:57:03,160
Rep. Julienne "Jam" L. Baronda: Mr. Speaker, currently po meron na po na inagurahan si Mr. President doon po sa Cavite

3916
04:57:03,160 --> 04:57:07,040
Rep. Julienne "Jam" L. Baronda: and there are CMP programs and programs po ng NHA.

3917
04:57:07,120 --> 04:57:11,040
Rep. Julienne "Jam" L. Baronda: Na meron na pong provision lahat po ng mga building nila.

3918
04:57:11,280 --> 04:57:17,740
Rep. Julienne "Jam" L. Baronda: What is good po ngayon, we adopted, kumbaga they adopted a green program po,

3919
04:57:17,920 --> 04:57:19,460
Rep. Julienne "Jam" L. Baronda: kasi last time hindi talaga pwede.

3920
04:57:19,660 --> 04:57:25,540
Rep. Julienne "Jam" L. Baronda: But now that's pwede, definitely po, gagawin po yun ng DSUD, Mr. Speaker.

3921
04:57:25,800 --> 04:57:29,260
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Yes po, maraming salamat po Madam Sponsor, Mr. Speaker.

3922
04:57:29,720 --> 04:57:35,880
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Related to that, bukod po dyan sa mga energy efficient homes,

3923
04:57:35,880 --> 04:57:41,620
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: ang atin din po ba, may mga plano rin po ba tayo, kasama din po sa mga plano natin,

3924
04:57:42,000 --> 04:57:47,000
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: yung mga tinatawag na mga climate resilient homes, disaster ready homes,

3925
04:57:47,180 --> 04:57:51,880
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: kasi given po naman na increasing frequency ng typhoons, ng pagbaha,

3926
04:57:53,080 --> 04:57:59,920
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: magkano po sa 2027 budget ng DSUD, ang nakapaloob dyan,

3927
04:58:00,060 --> 04:58:04,760
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: na naka-earmark po for climate resilient housing, if at all, kung meron lang po.

3928
04:58:04,760 --> 04:58:05,200
Rep. Julienne "Jam" L. Baronda: Mr. Speaker,

3929
04:58:05,880 --> 04:58:14,020
Rep. Julienne "Jam" L. Baronda: Definitely kasama na po dyan, to be resilient already, at naka-build-in na po sa total cost ng project per units, Mr. Speaker.

3930
04:58:15,260 --> 04:58:16,360
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Maraming salamat po.

3931
04:58:16,440 --> 04:58:27,320
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Ito po bang mga climate, pwede po bang makahingi ng halimbawa kung exactly ano itong mga climate resilient features that you have integrated in your housing units?

3932
04:58:31,000 --> 04:58:35,260
Rep. Julienne "Jam" L. Baronda: For example po, it was built already in mga non-flooded areas,

3933
04:58:35,260 --> 04:58:43,440
Rep. Julienne "Jam" L. Baronda: and meron po din tayo dun sa reset na pinuntahan ni Presidente sa Cavite, solar panel na din yun,

3934
04:58:44,060 --> 04:58:53,440
Rep. Julienne "Jam" L. Baronda: tapos yung proposal po dun sa Region 6 po ni NHA po, and ni DSUD po, naka-incorporate na po dyan.

3935
04:58:54,120 --> 04:59:04,940
Rep. Julienne "Jam" L. Baronda: Especially dun po sa mga areas na declared ng Project NOAA, and the low-lying areas po.

3936
04:59:04,940 --> 04:59:07,360
Rep. Julienne "Jam" L. Baronda: Or yung mga critical areas.

3937
04:59:07,520 --> 04:59:12,700
Rep. Julienne "Jam" L. Baronda: Kaya po, iniingi na rin natin yung suporta ng DNR for the support.

3938
04:59:14,080 --> 04:59:16,900
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Maraming salamat po, Madam Sponsor, Mr. Speaker.

3939
04:59:17,600 --> 04:59:29,620
